{'symbol': 'SNPS', 'date': '2019-11-20 22:30:00', 'title': 'Synopsys and AMD Execute Multi-Year ZeBu Emulation Agreement', 'text': "Synopsys, Inc. announced a multi-year agreement with AMD to utilize its ZeBu® Server 4 emulation system, accelerating verification of the growing number of AMD high-performance processor, graphics, and gaming projects. As part of this new agreement Synopsys will optimize its ZeBu and VCS® software for execution on AMD EPYC™ processor-based servers. AMD continues its development strategy to enable early customer enablement using the high-performance ZeBu emulation system. AMD and Synopsys will extend their successful emulation collaboration to support system-level debug and analog/mixed-signal emulation, in addition to software-driven power and performance analysis, hybrid emulation, and virtual host solutions. ZeBu Server 4 is the industry's fastest emulation system offering 2X higher performance over competitive solutions and a rich portfolio of virtual solutions. With its small footprint and one-tenth the power consumption compared to its largest competitor, ZeBu enables software and verification teams to efficiently scale their emulation farm to verify their most complex designs. ZeBu also enables companies to reduce the risk of missing critical power issues in their high-performance architectures by running actual customer application workloads rather than synthetic scenarios to validate performance and power requirements. Initial optimization results for VCS on the new EPYC 7002 series processor-based servers demonstrate a total cost of ownership reduction from a dual-socket to a single-socket server configuration while additionally improving simulation performance by greater than 30% as compared to executing the same design and testbench on a previous-generation EPYC 7000 series processor-based server."}
{'symbol': 'TGT', 'date': '2019-11-20 10:30:00', 'title': 'Target Posts Adjusted Earnings Per Share Of $1.36', 'text': "TARGET REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 EARNINGS.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.37 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.COMPANY RAISES FULL-YEAR EPS GUIDANCE.QTRLY COMPARABLE SALES INCREASE 4.5 PERCENT.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.36.Q3 REVENUE ROSE 4.7 PERCENT TO $18.7 BILLION.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $6.25 TO $6.45.SEES FY 2019 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $6.27 TO $6.47 FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.19, REVENUE VIEW $18.49 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q3 COMPARABLE DIGITAL CHANNEL SALES GREW 31%.FY EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $6.18 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.PLANS TO ISSUE A POST-HOLIDAY FINANCIAL UPDATE ON JANUARY 15, 2020.SEES Q4 COMPARABLE SALES GROWTH OF 3 TO 4 PERCENT.Q3 COMPARABLE TRAFFIC GREW 3.1%, DRIVEN BY INCREASES IN BOTH STORES AND DIGITAL CHANNELS.TARGET SAYS SAME-DAY FULFILLMENT SERVICES (ORDER PICK UP, DRIVE UP AND SHIPT) ACCOUNTED FOR 80% OF TARGET'S DIGITAL COMPARABLE SALES GROWTH IN QUARTER."}
